// (round 153, trim153) Trim Hearth: the features that can be switched off (Settings › Trim Hearth, Ctrl/⌘+K, the
// command bar). A switched-off feature's lazy groups never load: no code, no timers, no stand-in commands, Ctrl/⌘+K
// lines, keys-sheet lines, rail tools or app windows (lazy.js asks HearthFeatures.offGroups() once at the start).
// Its data stays where it is. The setting is this computer's own (localStorage 'hub.trim.off': a list of ids; never
// synced, never sent). Names, descriptions, usage words and the always-on (core) features are in trim-data.js (lazy
// group 'trim'), so the first screen only carries this list: 'id:group,group' separated by spaces ('id' alone: its one group has its name).
// A group that needs ('after') a switched-off group goes off with it, unless the need is only about order (SOFT).
